        "original_id": "cedbccd8-bd12-58a5-a92d-1d1583a914f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Hiwassee Dam, Fontana Dam, Hiwassee, North Carolina, Cherokee County, Swain County, Graham County, North Carolina, New York City\n- Systems: TVA system\n- Rivers and Reservoirs: Little Tennessee River, Hiwassee River, Hiwassee Reservoir\n- People: Billy Bland\n- Topics: dam height rankings, hydroelectric dams, village location, biography\n\nFacts:\n- Billy Bland was born on 5 April 1932 in Wilmington, North Carolina.\n- Hiwassee Dam is 307 feet tall and is the third highest dam in the TVA system, behind Fontana Dam and Watauga Dam.\n- Fontana Dam is a hydroelectric dam on the Little Tennessee River in Swain and Graham counties, North Carolina, United States.\n- Hiwassee is a small village in Cherokee County, North Carolina, beside Hiwassee Dam and the artificial Hiwassee Reservoir on the Hiwassee River.\n- Billy Bland was an American R&B singer and songwriter.\n- Billy Bland died on 22 March 2017 in New York City.",
